Developer Guide
===============

Eclipse
-------

Following the initial checkout, or after updating dependencies in the build.sbt file, run:

  activator "eclipse with-source=true"


Assets
------

When updating the bootstrap.js file, concatenate the "Modals", "Dropdowns", "Toggleable tabs" and the "Typeahead" plugins, 
and append the bootstrap-fileupload, bootstrap-datepicker and bootstrap-timepicker plugins.

When updating angular-custom.js, append angular-route and angular-sanitize. Remove any "//# sourceMappingURL" lines.

When updating highcharts.js, append highcharts-more.js and modules/exporting.js.

When updating moment.js, append moment-timezone-all-years.js.

When updating Font Awesome, use the unminified css version as the less file, and copy the font files to public/fonts/.

When updating highlight.js, create a custom package with support for bash and json, and copy styles/railscasts.css to 
app/assets/css/highlight-railscasts-x.y.less.


Tests
-----

To run all unit tests:

  activator "test-only *Test"

To run a specific test:
  
  activator "test-only com.zenobase.testing.BrowserTesting"

To skip webdriver tests, set -Dwebdriver.skip=true


Profiling
---------

1. Run the JVM that will be monitored with the following properties:

   -Dcom.sun.management.jmxremote \
   -Dcom.sun.management.jmxremote.port=1099 \
   -Dcom.sun.management.jmxremote.rmi.port=1099 \ 
   -Dcom.sun.management.jmxremote.authenticate=false \ 
   -Dcom.sun.management.jmxremote.ssl=false

2. Create an ssh tunnel (with dynamic port forwarding and listening on port 1999) to the remote machine. 

3. Configure jvisualvm or jmc to use localhost:1999 as a SOCKS proxy.

4. Create a JMX connection using the *internal* IP address of the remote machine, and port 1099.


Deploy Procedure
----------------

Use this procedure when there are no setup or configuration changes:

  1. Push the code to the build server.

  2. Obtain the build number [CircleCI].

  3. Update the build number in the stack settings [OpsWorks].

  4. Deploy the "Play" App to all machines in the Play Layer [OpsWorks].


Release Procedure
-----------------

Use this procedure when there are setup or configuration changes, but no database migration is required:

  1. Push zenobase-cookbooks to the build server.

  2. Obtain the build number [CircleCI].

  3. Update the "Repository URL" with the build number in the stack settings [OpsWorks].

  4. Push the application code to the build server.

  5. Obtain the build number [CircleCI].

  6. Update the build number in the stack settings [OpsWorks].

  7. Set up new instances [OpsWorks]:

     7.1. Add two m5.large instances named "{name}-1a" in us-east-1a and "{name}-1b" in us-east-1b to the "Elasticsearch" layer.

     7.2. Add the new instances to the "Play" layer.

  8. Start the new instances [OpsWorks].

  9. Wait for the status check to show 8 nodes and green health [Zenobase].

  10. Stop the old instances [OpsWorks].

  11. Wait for 4 nodes and green health [Zenobase].

  12. Tag HEAD with the build number.

  13. Cleanup (optional):

      13.1. Remove stopped instances [OpsWorks].

      13.2. Delete builds older than a month or so from the zeno-builds bucket [S3].

      13.3. Remove instances that are no longer reporting data [New Relic].


Migration Procedure
-------------------

Use this procedure to rebuild the database:

  1. Push the code to the build server.

  2. Obtain the build number [CircleCI].

  3. Update the build number in the stack settings [OpsWorks].

  4. Increment "elasticsearch.replay" and "clusterName" in the stack settings [OpsWorks].

  5. Set up new instances [OpsWorks]:

     4.1. Add two m5.large instances named "{name}-1a" in us-east-1a and "{name}-1b" in us-east-1b to the "Elasticsearch" layer.

     4.2. Add the new instances to the "Play" layer.

  6. Before proceeding:
  
     6.1. The status check must show 4 nodes and green health [Zenobase].

     6.2. There should be a recent snapshot.

  7. Start one of the new instances [OpsWorks].

  8. Switch the old cluster into read-only mode [Zenobase].

  9. Remove all old instances from the load balancer as soon as the new instances is listed as "in service" [EC2].

  10. Start other new instance [OpsWorks].

  11. Wait for the status check to show 4 nodes and green health [Zenobase].

  12. Stop the old instances [OpsWorks].

  13. Tag HEAD with the build number.

  14. Cleanup (optional):

      14.1. Remove stopped instances [OpsWorks].

      14.2. Delete builds older than a month or so from the zeno-builds bucket [S3].

      14.3. Remove instances that are no longer reporting data [New Relic].

      14.4. Remove all but the last few snapshot buckets [S3].


Restore Procedure
-----------------

  1. Bring up an empty elasticsearch instance.

  2. Register a snapshot repository, e.g.
  
    curl -XPUT 'localhost:9200/_snapshot/prod-xx' -d '{
      "type": "s3",
      "settings": {
          "bucket": "zeno-snapshots",
          "base_path": "prod-xx"
      }
    }'

  3. List snapshots:

    curl 'localhost:9200/_snapshot/prod-xx/_all?pretty=true'

  4. Restore a snapshot:

    curl -XPOST 'localhost:9200/_snapshot/prod-xx/yyyyyyyyyy/_restore'
